CREATED:20260717T141713Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260717T141713Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: NJ Bowling, Volleyball, Tennis & More
UID:event_315129933@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260722T033335Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T213000
SUMMARY:Bowling Night - North Jersey
DESCRIPTION:North Jersey Bowling\, Volleyball\, Tennis And More\nThis is a
 n event for casual bowling at Montvale Lanes\, 14 W. Grand Ave. All are we
 lcome for **two games\, food and drinks**\, and any post- or pre-game hang
  out. Show up anytime! Questions or comments? You can message Andy Milone 
 on Meetup\, or call/text him at **201-234-9609**.\n\n\\*\\*\\* Before bowl
 ing\, we might stop by the Pizza Parlour\, 6 S. Kinderkamack Road in Montv
 ale\, for a few slices. Post a comment on the event page to gauge interest
 . **After bowling\, we'll definitely be heading to Davey's Irish Pub & Res
 taurant\, 5 Park St. in Montvale\, or The Ridge Diner\, 125 Kinderkamack R
 oad in Park Ridge\, at 10 p.m. for some food and/or drinks.** \\*\\*\\*\n\
 nAbout the group: People of all ages\, backgrounds and abilities are welco
 me! We're not professionals and we're not in a league. In fact\, we're a g
 roup of people who probably each won't score more than 100 points and will
  land more than our fair share of gutter balls. There's no pressure at all
 !!!! We're not here to analyze your form or technique.\n\nMore event detai
 ls: You pay for your own games\, food and drinks. Please bring cash. The a
 lley does not accept card. But there is an ATM on site. **The** **cost per
  player is $18 for two games** **and bowling shoes.** If you have your own
  shoes\, the cost is $12. Please try to bring exact change since Andy will
  have a limited amount of cash. If you bring a $20 bill and he doesn't hav
 e change\, any remainder would just go toward the bowling alley tip.\n\nFo
 od and drinks (alcoholic and non-alcoholic) are available on site\, plus t
 ables and an alley bar to hang at during the event. There is a dart board 
 and a few arcade games\, as well.\n\n**What do you do when you get there?*
 * First\, find the group inside around the front desk. Look for a growing 
 group of people! Call or text Andy Milone at 201-234-9609 if you can't fin
 d us. Once Andy secures the lanes\, please pay him before getting your bow
 ling shoes.\n\n**Please know that it is possible we have to wait 20-40 min
 utes until lane(s) free up.** It's also possible that we may have to reloc
 ate or cancel that night if there's a long wait list upon arrival. Please 
 keep that in mind if traveling from far away!\n\nFor those who don't have 
 cars or are looking to avoid driving\, the Montvale Train Station is only 
 like a five-minute walk from the bowling alley and can be reached via the 
 Pascack Valley Line. Last train leaves at 12:20 a.m. and heads toward Hobo
 ken. (https://gmtma.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/11/rail_system_map.jpg)\n\
 nMany thanks to Taylor\, one of our group participants\, for recommending 
 Montvale Lanes! You can learn more at: www.montvalelanes.com.\n\nHope you'
 ll join us for our 25th bowling event\, or consider attending one of our v
 olleyball\, ping pong\, skating or other activities -> www.meetup.com/nort
 h-jersey-bowling-soccer-volleyball\n\nIf interested in staying touch with 
 group members or conversing about future events\, feel free to inquire abo
 ut our WhatsApp group chat.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/north-jersey-bowling-soccer-volleybal
 l/events/315129933/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260606T061447Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260606T061447Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: NJ Bowling, Volleyball, Tennis & More
UID:event_315550790@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260722T033335Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260725T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260725T120000
SUMMARY:Weekend Warrior Tennis (Saturdays)
DESCRIPTION:North Jersey Bowling\, Volleyball\, Tennis And More\nWe meet a
 t 9AM unless one or more people comment wanting to meet at 8AM which is my
  preferred time. You’re welcome to show up any time but are encouraged t
 o post it so we have a better idea of what to expect for that day. (Those 
 who share the same comment for start time can simply like that comment so 
 we see how many show up for that time without potentially cluttering the c
 omments.)\n\n**RULES:** By signing up you agree to follow these rules:\n\n
 1\\. No instruction or orders are allowed on any of our group courts\\. If
  two or more people are in agreement then they’re welcome to exchange in
 structions so long as they relinquish their court positions and don’t di
 srupt active players\\. If anyone is instructing or ordering you and you
 ’re not comfortable then please tell them or let me know\\. Everyone sho
 uld feel free to play however they wish without being directed without agr
 eement\\\, most especially beginners\\.\n\n2\\. No formal matches are allo
 wed on any of our group\\-reserved courts\\. If people are in agreement th
 en they’re welcome to find another court not in use by our group to play
  strict matches\\. If we need to rotate people in and out due to lack of e
 nough courts then we’ll follow my Florida instructor’s method for bala
 nced clinic matches\\. This will typically include quick matches to 5 poin
 ts after which everyone rotates clockwise one position\\. This keeps those
  waiting rotated back in often and also discourages team clotting\\.\n\n3\
 \. We are foremost beginner\\-friendly and not aggressively competitive or
  an instruction\\-oriented group\\. A little light and friendly competitio
 n or giving a quick tip so long as you’re not holding up the court is OK
  but please pace yourself against the person you’re hitting to \\(e\\.g\
 \. hit softer to members that might not be as good or as aggressive as you
 \\)\\. Everyone should be made to feel welcome and free regardless of skil
 l level\\. Beginners most especially should always feel comfortable here\\
 .\n\n4\\. Please make sure you’re signed up using a name that matches yo
 ur Meetup name\\. New players should always check in with me so I can mark
  you down as having checked in\\. Anyone showing up without a Meetup RSVP 
 will be asked to do so before they can participate in the event\\. If you
 ’re bringing one guest that’s fine\\\, just make sure to mark them on 
 your RSVP\\.\n\n5\\. If I feel you’re consistently not following the rul
 es I have the right to ask you to relinquish your position on the court\\.
  Please don’t sign up and attend if you don’t agree to following any o
 ne rule here\\. We are largely democratic but I reserve the right to make 
 any final calls if I deem it necessary for any reason\\\, such as breaking
  up and remixing long\\-locked groups if we have more than one court\\.\n\
 n**EQUIPMENT:** Please bring your own racquet and water\, as we don’t pr
 ovide those. I always have some balls for at least one court\, but feel fr
 ee to bring your own in case we need to branch out over more than one cour
 t.\n\n**DISCLAIMER:** Courts are subject to availability and weather. If y
 ou make plans to attend please be prepared to cancel or adjust our locatio
 n as needed. Furthermore\, by attending you agree to be fully responsible 
 for your own health and safety. Each person is responsible to take a break
  for rest and water at their own discretion.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/north-jersey-bowling-soccer-volleybal
 l/events/315550790/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260704T233430Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260704T233430Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
